// Phase 13 Plan 04 Task 2 -- D-13-28's criterion-3 twin pair, ALPHA
// half. A shared callee (`sink`) with two callers (`alpha`, `beta`):
// both borrow their own parameter, call `sink` (which takes ownership
// of its OWN parameter internally -- deriveFunctionUsesParam-shaped
// consumption, D-08-02), then, in the clean base, take their own
// buffer back only AFTER the call -- the call is the loan's own last
// use (D-13-09b's callIsLastUse backward gate), so both check clean.
//
// InterproceduralLoanInjector's marker sits on ALPHA's own take
// statement; Inject swaps it with its immediately preceding statement
// (the call), reproducing 13-01's own empirically-verified swap-fixable
// defect (derivation_interprocedural_loan_defect.lang) -- but now
// inside a shared-callee, two-caller topology, reached from `main`
// through a depth-2 relay chain (root-to-detection hop distance 2,
// D-13-26.2). `beta` carries no marker and is never mutated by this
// plan's injector run, so it stays clean regardless.
//
// D-13-28's full criterion -- a driver applying the identical mutation
// to BOTH alpha and beta, then observing that only a shared-callee
// (`sink`) edit re-checks the WHOLE program clean, while a per-caller
// swap-fix only ever clears the one caller it touched -- is exercised
// by a later plan's repair/driver test (13-05/13-06), once
// wrap_call_in_try's sibling repairs exist. This plan's own obligation
// is narrower and fully met here: the base checks clean unmutated, and
// the injector run against EITHER caller alone produces exactly one
// check.interprocedural_loan_liveness diagnostic (D-13-26.3). See
// heldout_shared_callee_twin_mirror.lang for the mirror half, where the
// marked (and therefore reachable, depth-2) caller is `beta` instead --
// the control against a rule that always blames a fixed caller
// position regardless of which function the defect is actually in.

module phase13.heldout_shared_callee_twin_alpha

export {
  fn main
}

fn sink(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let held = take buffer
  held
}

fn alpha(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let routed = sink(borrowed)
  let delivered = take buffer // lang:interprocedural-loan-target
  routed
}

fn beta(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let routed = sink(borrowed)
  let delivered = take buffer
  routed
}

fn relay(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let out = alpha(buffer)
  out
}

fn main(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let out = relay(buffer)
  out
}
